t</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do the uratha do during this era?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, the same thing they do now. Apocalypse might be the better choice, since there seems to be more of an established history for them at that point. Though I'm sure a Forsaken can could come up with some cool stuff for them in a homebrew. And we should be getting a small paragraph about the status of werewolves in the Neolithic Mage section of the Dark Eras book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T12:53:28-08:00","id":425576,"title":"","content":"Yeah I was just thinking that myself, I'll jump the era over to the alocalypse forum. And the damned iPhone double posted it soon as I opened my internets &gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T14:14:58-08:00","id":425660,"title":"","content":"I'd actually vote for doing the era with Forsaken over Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> Stone age Apocalypse seems like it would be... kind of boring. Almost all of the big conflicts of WtA are absent. The only big difference would be more time spent fighting other Gaian Garou over territory and such; since the Weaver and Wyrm aren't nearly as problematic yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T14:49:19-08:00","id":425701,"title":"","content":"Aren't problematic at all for the time. How far back is the gauntlet rending in forsaken?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T15:01:16-08:00","id":425708,"title":"","content":"The earliest mention I can recall of werewolves doing their thing is when they were crossing the ice bridge alongside humans. So if the Sundering happened and we're working on linear time, it was before that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T19:54:40-08:00","id":426069,"title":"","content":"With Forsaken right around the corner I may stick with apocalypse until I can read through the book completely. Besides deluxe botw20th is almost upon me and I've got story teller screens I want to use. The idea is a multi generational story arc, moving through different eras until a confrontation in modern nights. The what is pretty rad, trying to think of an enemy that can encompass that is the difficult part. The wyrm involvement in the world makes that real easy. Meta plots are fun like that. Forsaken... might work with the hosts? Could be rival bloodlines of forsaken, pure vs forsaken or even a very persistent bale hound cult... the beginning being vague makes it a touch on the arduous side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}